  "description": "Sub-division of site and erection of a detached dwelling house at rear, with associated parking, landscaping and amenity space and resurfacing of access road",
  "title_number": [],
  "site_number": "72",
  "lapsed_date": "10/10/2025",
  "lpa_name": "Enfield",
  "uprn": "000207111126",
  "appeal_status": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by virtue of its siting, size, design, footprint, bulk and massing  would appear as a cramped and discordant form of development which is out of keeping with the overall pattern of development and fails to harmonise with the existing residential character, detrimental to the visual amenities of the surrounding area. The proposals are thereby contrary to the advice contained within the National Planning Policy Framework 2021, Policies GG2, D3, D4 and D8 of the London Plan (2021); Policy CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010) and Policies DMD6, DMD7, DMD8, and DMD37 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).",
    "Insufficient information has been submitted to demonstrate that the proposed development would not adversely impact upon existing mature trees, which are prominent and offer valuable amenity within the local landscape and contribute towards the character and appearance of the local environment. The proposal would therefore be contrary to the advice contained within the NPPF and  NPPG, Policies D3 and G7 of the London Plan (2021), policies CP31 and CP34 of the Core Strategy and policy DMD80 of the Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposed development, by virtue of the unacceptable overlooking from adjacent occupiers to the proposed amenity space would result in sub-standard form of accommodation detrimental to the residential amneities of future occupiers, contrary to Policies D4 and D6 of the London Plan 2021, the Nationally Described Space Standards 2015, Policies CP4 and CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy 2010 and Policies DMD7, DMD8, DMD9 and DMD10 of the Enfield Development Management Document 2014.",
    "The proposed development would prejudice the implementation approved parking details submitted in respect of planning application 21/02192/FUL for the  conversion of 72 Norfolk Road into 4 x self-contained flats involving part single, part 2-storey side and rear extension, single storey rear extension and the absence of planning permission to regularise the planning position in respect of this matter the proposal would give rise to conditions prejudicial to highway and pedestrian safety contrary to Policies T5 and T6 of the London Plan (2021): Policies CP24 and CP25 of the Enfield Core Strategy 2010 and Policies DMD45, DMD47 and DMD48 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014)."
  ],
